  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Client's Own Poster",
    "overview": "- **Direction:** the classic accommodation page, which the client picked on 2026-11-12. It is played straight, at full craft, in the client's own brand (brand guide, Edition 1).\n- **The poster recipe** (brand guide p10) drives every surface:\n  - a Cream or marble field;\n  - a gold-framed warm photo;\n  - a gold headline bar;\n  - bold Arimo amenities;\n  - the Midnight Navy contact bar at the bottom edge.\n- **Craft bar:** The Menhaden (persistent booking dock), Relais Rossar (warm, framed restraint) and Grano Hotels (dates picker as the hero's working action). See `docs/planning/design-references.md`.\n\nThe system is warm, square-shouldered and quiet. Gold is structure: bars, frames, rules and line icons. Navy does the work: actions, links, the contact bar and the phone dock. The public site is sparse and centred on phones and two-column on desktop. The dashboard is denser: white panels on a Chalk canvas, with Arimo titles. The brand's gold, navy and Cream come through there in small, exact doses.\n\nThe way out of the cream-and-gold look AI tools default to is fidelity to the client's poster, not a different palette (Decision 1). The direction contract rejects three looks: a generic hotel chain, safari-lodge clichés, and anything over-luxurious.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Cream grounds with Marble White panels; gold frames and rules; navy anchors at the foot.",
      "Josefin Sans capitals for headings and labels; Arimo for everything people read; Sacramento once, large and gold.",
      "2–4 px corners everywhere, matching the square gold frames.",
      "Soft shadows under 8% opacity, always over an edge.",
      "One motion flourish, a gold sheen after first interaction, and none under reduced motion.",
      "Placeholders that say they are placeholders."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Gold Is Structure Rule",
        "body": "Gold frames, divides and decorates. Navy (on light) and Cream (on navy) are the only interactive colours. No button, link or selected state is filled gold (Decision 5).",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Text-Gold Rule",
        "body": "Gold that must be read on a light ground is Gold Text, never Romaic Gold or Deep Gold.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The On-Dark Rule",
        "body": "Inside the `.on-dark` recipe (`src/app/globals.css`), the role colours flip by themselves: text white, secondary Cream, links white with Champagne hover, focus Champagne. Dark surfaces use the recipe rather than hand-set colours.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One Script Rule",
        "body": "Sacramento appears at most once per view, large and gold.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Bold Arimo On Gold Rule",
        "body": "Text on a gold bar is bold Arimo in ink, never Josefin capitals (brand guide p8, p10; Decision 2).",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Tracking Lives In Recipes Rule",
        "body": "Letter-spacing belongs to the Josefin recipes, not the size tokens, so Arimo titles at the same sizes keep normal spacing.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Edge First Rule",
        "body": "Every shadow sits on something that already has an edge: a hairline, a control border or a gold frame. Shadows stay under 8% opacity on light grounds.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do follow the poster recipe (brand guide p10): Cream or marble field, gold-framed photo, gold headline bar, bold Arimo amenities, navy contact bar at the foot.",
      "Do frame every photo with the 4 px Romaic Gold frame, and label every stand-in on its face.",
      "Do use Gold Text for gold-coloured type and icons on light grounds, and Romaic Gold only on navy or as structure.",
      "Do use gold rules (2 px gradient, or Romaic Gold at 60% inside panels) as dividers on public surfaces.",
      "Do wrap dark surfaces in the `.on-dark` recipe so links, focus and text flip together.",
      "Do keep every interactive border at the control colour (4.0:1), and give every control a 44 px target.",
      "Do gate motion behind first interaction and `prefers-reduced-motion`. Animate only transform and opacity."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't retype the wordmark in any font, redraw the corner marks, or recolour, stretch, shadow or rotate the logo (brand guide p4). Use `LogoSlot` until the PNGs arrive.",
      "Don't fill buttons, links or selected states with gold. Gold is never interactive.",
      "Don't set gold-bar text in Josefin capitals.",
      "Don't use Romaic Gold or Deep Gold as text on Cream or white.",
      "Don't use the corner-mark accents (purple, coral, teal) as UI colours.",
      "Don't put eyebrow labels above headings. The brand guide's \"02 — BRAND OVERVIEW\" numbering stays in the PDF (Decision 3).",
      "Don't imitate the marble texture or the palm leaf in CSS.",
      "Don't mark the current nav row with a side stripe. Use the tint, the weight and the gold icon.",
